\f1\b\fs26 \cf2 \strokec2 Key gaps in the synthetic generator's match to reality:
\f0\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Trend slope is 3.5\'d7 too strong
\f0\b0 \'a0\'97 the synthetic data has trends ~3.5\'d7 steeper than the real data. This means the detector is being trained on unrealistically large trend signals; it may either overfit to large slopes and miss subtle real-world trends, or the trend thresholds may be calibrated too aggressively.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Weekly seasonality is only 35% of the real data
\f0\b0 \'a0\'97 the synthetic data is\'a0
\f2\i far
\f0\i0 \'a0too smooth across days-of-week. The real data has ~3\'d7 stronger day-of-week patterns. The detector will likely under-detect or mis-characterize weekly patterns when applied to real data.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Yearly seasonality and diff kurtosis are borderline
\f0\b0 \'a0(both ~0.58\'960.59 ratio). The synthetic data has substantially thinner tails (kurtosis) and weaker annual cycles than reality, meaning rare extreme events and annual patterns are underrepresented in training.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 ACF values are slightly too high
\f0\b0 \'a0(0.987 vs 0.955). The synthetic data is slightly "smoother" / more autocorrelated than reality, which could make the detector under-sensitive to real-world short-horizon volatility.\
